 "text": "Hi! How are you doing right now? Try to stay as dry as possible. If the storm hits while you're set up, pitch a tarp inside the tent as the primary cover, and only after that as a back up. That's a decent distance, but wind can make the lightning come much closer. Lightning can travel through the tent rope, so take them down if the storm gets rough. Sorry, I can't. That's something only the host can do. If the storm gets bad, yes. If not, leave it up and continue with your day. Find a low spot under a tree and pitch a tarp. Then make a fire if it's not raining too hard. Then get inside and keep the tent door closed. Keep a fire going the roof.",
